  "description": "OXERHD10 crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C110 H202 Er8 O33. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er1F (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2F (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3F (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4F (Er) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.426-4.479 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.15-145.88°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Er8O(thd)10(OH)12. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
